admin-cache-title = Cache maintenance
admin-cache-help = By default, cached email content expires after 60 days without use. Opening an expired message downloads its content again. Original messages, drafts and protected local content are preserved.
admin-cache-expiry = Cached message lifetime
admin-cache-orphans = Unreferenced bodies and space reclamation
admin-cache-advanced = Batch limits and timing
admin-cache-settings-help = Changes use the normal administrator settings policy, validation and audit trail.
admin-cache-expiry-enabled = Automatically expire cached message bodies
admin-cache-retention-days = Days without use before expiry
admin-cache-expiry-status = Cached body expiry
admin-cache-expiry-result = Scanned: { $scanned } · Detached cache references: { $detached } · Protected: { $protected }
admin-cache-expiry-help = Only bodies confirmed to be recoverable from an upstream mailbox are eligible. Scans and header refreshes do not renew the inactivity lease.
admin-cache-inspect = Inspect cache storage
admin-cache-inspect-help = Open database observability to measure cached payload, referenced bodies and orphaned copies.
admin-cache-no-status = No expiry batch has completed in this server process.
admin-cache-settings-unavailable = Cache settings could not be loaded.
admin-cache-change-log = Sync history
admin-cache-change-log-help = Old change records expire after 60 days by default. Clients using older sync tokens receive a full-resync response.
admin-cache-no-sources = No connected mailbox currently has a confirmed refetch path. Protected content is kept.
admin-cache-wal-recycled = Recycled allocated WAL space; cleanup can continue.
admin-cache-wal-recovery = Cleanup is waiting for WAL recovery or checkpointing. Pending journal data is preserved.

admin-cache-removed-payload = Cached payload removed
admin-cache-oversized = Large bodies deferred
admin-cache-change-removed = Sync-history rows removed

admin-cache-parsed-copies = Parsed body copies cleared
admin-cache-parsed-bytes = Parsed body data removed
admin-cache-change-chunked = Sync states cleaned in chunks

# Public static representations only; process-local counters.
admin-cache-assets-title = Public static asset RAM cache
admin-cache-assets-clear = Clear static cache
admin-cache-assets-help = Retains public assets only. The budget covers owned resident payloads, not in-flight responses or process RSS. Deployed shell and service-worker bytes may remain cached for the configured revalidation interval.
admin-cache-assets-clear-help = Clearing releases retained entries; active responses finish normally. Enabled preload may refill the cache. Counters cover this server process.
admin-cache-assets-stale = Policy refresh failed; the last applied configuration remains active.
admin-cache-assets-applied = Configuration applied: { $time }
admin-cache-assets-resident = Owned payload / budget
admin-cache-assets-entries = Entries / limit
admin-cache-assets-file = Effective owned file limit
admin-cache-assets-loads = Running / limit; queued / limit
admin-cache-assets-hits = Hits / accepted loads / shared waiters
admin-cache-assets-evictions = Evicted / expired / oversized bypasses
admin-cache-assets-failures = Busy refusals / failed worker jobs
admin-cache-assets-preload = Preload mode; retained / skipped

admin-cache-assets-encoded = Encoded payload / owned portion
admin-cache-assets-encoding-loads = Verified sidecars / generated encodings
admin-cache-assets-encoding-help = Public static encodings share the cache budget. Sidecars are checked against raw bytes; adapted assets may be encoded once on a bounded cache miss. Mail, API data and private HTML are excluded.
admin-cache-prepared-title = Prepared mail metadata cache
admin-cache-prepared-help = Prepared metadata only; each response still needs fresh source and authorization checks.
admin-cache-prepared-enabled = Enable prepared metadata
admin-cache-prepared-budgetMiB = RAM budget (MiB)
admin-cache-prepared-maxEntries = Maximum cached pages
admin-cache-prepared-maxAccounts = Maximum accounts
admin-cache-prepared-idleSeconds = Idle retention (seconds)
admin-cache-prepared-limits = Held and evicted results remain charged. Parser, SQL and RSS memory are separate. Defaults are not sized for 10,000 users.
admin-cache-prepared-refresh = Saved policy applies before the next eligible preparation after publication. Disabling invalidates old candidates; refresh to inspect this process.
admin-cache-prepared-refresh-status = Refresh status
admin-cache-prepared-memory = Charged RAM / budget
admin-cache-prepared-residents = Pages / limit; accounts / limit
admin-cache-prepared-work = Admitted / 16; active / 2; pending
admin-cache-prepared-results = Hits / misses / builds / evictions
admin-cache-prepared-seeds = Seed calls / rows; invalidation errors
admin-cache-prepared-invalid = Enter every field within its displayed bounds, with no additional fields.
admin-cache-prepared-unknown = Not observed
